    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Generate distinct cold-email infrastructure domain candidates for brand \"{{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.fields.Name }}\". Their real domain is \"{{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.fields.domain }}\" - never propose it.\n\nReturn FOUR groups:\n\nGROUP A - PREFIX (50 .com candidates):\nWord before brand or shortened brand. Words to consider: get, try, use, go, meet, join, run, with, hq, co, the, hey, my, our, ship, build, make, real, just, on.\n\nGROUP B - SUFFIX (50 .com candidates):\nWord after brand. Words to consider: hq, app, co, labs, now, team, ops, pro, hub, works, studio, factory, kit, suite, base, stack, world.\n\nGROUP C - ABBREVIATED (50 .com candidates):\nFirst shorten or modify the brand: remove vowels, use initials, combine syllables, drop letters, or recombine parts. THEN add a prefix or suffix from the lists above. Examples for \"Salesforce\": sfops, getsalesf, salesfwerks, sforcehub, salez-co.\n\nGROUP D - INFO (50 .info branded candidates):\nBranded .info domains. Each must be brand-adjacent (use the brand, an abbreviated brand, or brand + prefix/suffix from the lists above) and end with .info. Mix prefix, suffix, and abbreviated styles. Examples: getacme.info, acmehq.info, acmops.info, acme-co.info, tryacme.info.\n\nCRITICAL - COMMON BRAND RULE:\nIf the brand name is a common English word, a very short name, or a well-known brand (likely all \"get<brand>\", \"<brand>app\", \"<brand>hq\" patterns are taken), then HEAVILY bias toward GROUP C (creative abbreviated forms) and unusual prefix/suffix combinations. For these brands do NOT propose the obvious \"get<brand>\" or \"<brand>hq\" in the .com groups - go straight to creative variants. The .info group can still use the obvious patterns because .info availability is not a concern.\n\nRules:\n- Groups A, B, C are ALL .com (every candidate ends with .com)\n- Group D is ALL .info (every candidate ends with .info)\n- All pronounceable\n- Brand-adjacent and recognizable\n- Never propose the real domain\n- No duplicates across groups\n- Lowercase only, no hyphens unless essential\n- Return exactly 50 + 50 + 50 + 50 = 200 candidates\n\nReturn ONLY the JSON object with the four arrays. No prose, no commentary.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a brand-aware domain ideation assistant. You generate dense, creative .com and .info domain lists and return strictly structured JSON."
        }
      },
